  "scope": "Eight-step Buck, Buck/Boost CCM comparison, four topology applications and standalone ADC signal-chain calculator; not whole-project retirement; two stateless OP step/sine labs (no formal assessment); six static OP concept lessons (one documented bandwidth wording correction; no assessment); stateless three-case OP formative diagnosis (no certification); OP DC Level 0–5 trainer with guarded browser-local mastery, not official assessment; OP AMP Slew Rate first-attempt, transfer and 1/7/30/90-day review in existing V5 Evidence (not BOARD_PASS); C2000 ADC five-lesson read-only course referencing existing ADC calculator, with no old progress migration; ADC formal 3 question families (levels/codes, divider power, signed-current offset), source V5 first-attempt/transfer/retention; no alternative scoring store; SPI three-family first attempt/changed-condition transfer/1/7/30/90-day retention backed by existing V5 Evidence; not actual hardware validation or all remaining formal families; Buck three-family formal first-attempt/transfer/1/7/30/90-day retention in existing V5 Evidence; no separate grade or BOARDS_PASS. Four original power-topology formal families (PFC/PSFB/LLC/inverter) first attempt, B/C transfer and D/1/7/30/90 retention now use the existing sole V5 Evidence owner; no new physics, grade store or BOARD_PASS; the remaining source modules and rights Issue #20 are still open. Assessment V8 exposes all nine original V8 base families, including AFE then ACMC. Numeric open responses, diagnostic games, hardware validation, publication rights and retirement remain separate.",
